WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
In the Acts of the Apostles,
Peter tells a crowd:

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.810
repent and be baptised, every one of you.

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.130
Then he adds: the promise is
to you and to your children.

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.140
Later in Acts, a jailer
is baptised in the night,

5
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.150
with all his household.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.010
Were there babies in that house?

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.930
The text does not say.

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.190
So should a baby be baptised
before it can choose,

9
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.330
or wait until a person can say yes?

10
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.140
In this mission, you'll read what
the New Testament says about baptism,

11
00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.270
and what it leaves unsaid.

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.770
Then you'll see why Christians who all
baptise still disagree about who should

13
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.150
be baptised.

14
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.840
Your mission: weigh up the
arguments for baptising babies,

15
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:42.920
and for waiting.
